  "Main topic of the publication": "This study investigates the innate immunity of Hofbauer cells from placentae obtained at early/mid-gestation (18–21.6 weeks) and term (>37 weeks) when exposed to HIV and CMV. The study reveals the dynamic nature of placental immunity and underscores the need for targeted interventions to address unique immune and metabolic disruptions caused by viral infections at distinct stages of pregnancy to improve fetal and infant health outcomes.",
